    "# Team 7 · Monday: a material-finder autoencoder (MINC-2500)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Team:** Ugo, Alvaro, Sneha · **Hackathon:** AI Methods I, 16–20 November 2026\n",
    "\n",
    "**App idea:** a user uploads a photo of a surface (facade, floor, wall finish). The app returns the **5 most similar material patches**, a **material guess** and a warning if the photo looks **unusual** for a building material.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Use of the autoencoder:** similarity search in latent space (main), anomaly score from the reconstruction error (bonus).\n",
    "\n",
    "| Section | What happens |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| 1 | Load MINC-2500, keep 13 building materials, 64 × 64 RGB |\n",
    "| 2 | Two architectures: dense AE and convolutional AE |\n",
    "| 3 | Three setups on the same split and seed, one table (MSE + precision@5) |\n",
    "| 4 | Similarity search: the proof figure, per-material quality, UMAP |\n",
    "| 5 | Bonus: \"unusual photo\" score (building materials vs everything else) |\n",
    "| 6 | Export for the model server: ONNX, config, gallery, examples |\n",
    "| 7 | Conclusions (write them yourselves after the full run) |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Data:** MINC-2500, Hugging Face mirror [`mcimpoi/minc-2500_split_1`](https://huggingface.co/datasets/mcimpoi/minc-2500_split_1), CC BY 4.0. Cite: Bell, Upchurch, Snavely and Bala (2015), *Material Recognition in the Wild with the Materials in Context Database*, CVPR.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Before you run:** the parquet files must be in `data/minc-2500/data/` at the **root of the repository** (git-ignored). Download once with:\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "hf download mcimpoi/minc-2500_split_1 --repo-type dataset --local-dir data/minc-2500\n",
    "```"
   ]
