    "# 1. The data\n",
    "\n",
    "MINC-2500 has 23 classes of 2,500 patches each (362 × 362 px). We keep the **13 building materials** for training. The 10 other classes (food, foliage, sky, skin…) are never used for training: we only use their **test** patches in section 5, as examples of \"not a building material\".\n",
    "\n",
    "**Split:** we use the train / validation / test split that comes with the dataset (split 1). The same split and seed for every setup.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Preprocessing** (the server on Tuesday must do exactly the same, so it is one function):\n",
    "1. convert to RGB;\n",
    "2. centre-crop to a square (MINC patches are already square; user photos are not);\n",
    "3. resize to 64 × 64 with bilinear filtering;\n",
    "4. pixels 0–255 → 0–1, shape (3, 64, 64).\n",
    "\n",
    "We keep the images as **uint8** in memory (4× less than float) and convert each batch when we use it."
   ]
