    "# 2. Two architectures\n",
    "\n",
    "- **DenseAE:** flattens the 64 × 64 × 3 = 12,288 numbers and squeezes them through a hidden layer of 256 to the code. It ignores that neighbouring pixels belong together: our baseline.\n",
    "- **ConvAE:** three stride-2 convolutions halve the image 64 → 32 → 16 → 8, then a linear layer makes the code. The decoder mirrors it with transposed convolutions. A `Sigmoid` at the end keeps the output pixels in 0–1.\n",
    "\n",
    "Both have an `encoder` (image → code) and a `decoder` (code → image). The **code** (latent vector) is what we use for similarity search."
