    "**✍️ Interpret honestly:** reconstruction error measures *how hard a picture is to rebuild*, not *what it is*. Smooth classes (sky, water) may be rebuilt **easily** and slip through; busy textures (foliage, hair) stand out. If the ROC AUC is low, say so: in the app, show the score as a hint, not a verdict."
=======
    "# 5. Bonus: an \"unusual photo\" score\n",
    "\n",
    "The app should warn when a photo is not a building-material surface at all (a face, a plate of food, the sky). The autoencoder was trained only on building materials, so it should rebuild those better than anything else.\n",
    "\n",
    "1. The **threshold** is the 95th percentile of the reconstruction error on **validation** building patches: about 5% false alarms by design.\n",
    "2. We test it **once** on test patches: building materials (normal) vs the 10 other MINC classes (unusual), which the model never saw."
   ]
